ANALYSIS:
- The rule accesses SBOM data from both SPDX and CycloneDX formats through the `lib.sbom` library, combining them into a single array using `array.concat`
- The rule checks if no SBOM attestations exist by counting the combined SBOM array and triggering a violation when the count equals zero
- The core validation logic triggers a violation when `not konflux.is_validating_image_index` AND `count(_sboms) == 0`, meaning no SBOMs are found for non-image-index builds
- The result is generated using `lib.result_helper` with the rule metadata chain and an empty array as the violation details, producing a deny decision with the configured failure message

RULE:
```rego
package sbom

import rego.v1
import data.lib
import data.lib.konflux

_sboms := array.concat(lib.sbom.spdx_sboms, lib.sbom.cyclonedx_sboms)

# METADATA
# title: Found
# description: Confirm an SBOM attestation exists.
# custom:
#   short_name: found
#   failure_msg: No SBOM attestations found
#   solution: >-
#     Make sure the build process produces an SBOM attestation.
#   collections:
#   - minimal
#   - redhat
deny contains result if {
	# TODO: Workaround until Konflux produces SBOMs for Image Indexes:
	# https://issues.redhat.com/browse/KONFLUX-4330
	not konflux.is_validating_image_index

	count(_sboms) == 0
	result := lib.result_helper(rego.metadata.chain(), [])
}
