ANALYSIS:
- The rule accesses SLSA Provenance attestations through `lib.pipelinerun_attestations` and extracts task information using `tekton.tasks(att)`
- The rule iterates over each task in the attestations and checks if the task reference is pinned using `tekton.task_ref(task).pinned`
- The core validation logic triggers a violation when a task reference is NOT pinned (the `not tekton.task_ref(task).pinned` condition is true)
- The result is generated using `lib.result_helper_with_term` which creates a structured failure message including the task name and pipeline task name that caused the violation

RULE:
```rego
package tasks

import rego.v1
import data.lib
import data.lib.json as j
import data.lib.tekton

# METADATA
# title: Pinned Task references
# description: >-
#   Ensure that all Tasks in the SLSA Provenance attestation use an immuntable reference to the
#   Task definition.
# custom:
#   short_name: pinned_task_refs
#   failure_msg: Task %s is used by pipeline task %s via an unpinned reference.
#   solution: >-
#     Make sure the build pipeline uses Tasks via pinned references. For example, if the git
#     resolver is used, use a commit ID instead of a branch name.
#   collections:
#   - redhat
#   depends_on:
#   - tasks.pipeline_has_tasks
#
deny contains result if {
	some att in lib.pipelinerun_attestations
	some task in tekton.tasks(att)
	not tekton.task_ref(task).pinned
	result := lib.result_helper_with_term(
		rego.metadata.chain(),
		[tekton.task_name(task), tekton.pipeline_task_name(task)],
		tekton.task_name(task),
	)
}
```

